{# The front door the category pages never had. Council corner has /council/,
   roadworks has /roadworks/; the directory had nine pages hanging off nothing
   but a row of chips at the foot of the home page.

   Each category shows what is actually in it, so nobody clicks into an empty
   list to find out. The "getting listed" invitation lives here once rather
   than being repeated nine times. #}

<section class="wrap council-page" aria-labelledby="page-title">
  <div class="rule" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  <p class="page-intro">A list of what is in the town, put together by hand.
  Listings are free and always will be — there is nothing to pay to appear and
  no way to pay for a better position. Everything is alphabetical.</p>

  <div class="dir-index">
    {% for cat in directory.categories %}
    <a class="dir-index-item" href="/directory/{{ cat.slug }}/">
      <span class="dir-index-label">{{ cat.label | safe }}</span>
      <span class="dir-index-sub">
        {%- if cat.entries.length %}{{ cat.entries.length }}
        {%- elif cat.open %}open
        {%- else %}0{% endif -%}
      </span>
    </a>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>

  <div class="rule" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  <h2>Getting listed</h2>
  <p>If you run something in Largs that should be here, drop us an email at
  <a href="mailto:hello@largs.scot?subject=Directory%20listing">hello@largs.scot</a>
  with your name, what you do, where you are and a way to get in touch. We'll
  check it's current and put it up. It's free, and it stays free.</p>

  <h2>Who have we missed?</h2>
  <p>This is built by hand, so there'll be gaps — several categories are empty
  and the rest are incomplete. If we've missed you, or something's moved,
  closed or changed, let us know and we'd be glad to hear.</p>
</section>
